  "response": "잠들기 직전에 낮의 대화들이 자꾸 떠오르는 거, 그 상태가 얼마나 피곤하고 답답할지 짐작이 갑니다. 오래 이어져 왔다고 하셨는데, 그때 떠오르는 대화들 안에서는 보통 어떤 감정이나 생각이 더 크게 느껴지나요?",
  "reasoning": "The user wants me to respond as a counselor in Korean. Let me analyze what the client said:\n\n- They mentioned that insomnia is their biggest problem\n- When they lie down to sleep, conversations from the day keep replaying in their mind\n- They said it's been going on for a while (\"오래됐어요\")\n\nWhat's appropriate here:\n- Acknowledge the difficulty of this experience\n- Not rush to solutions or minimize it\n- Show that I understand the specific mechanism they described (replaying conversations)\n- Maybe gently explore the emotional tone or what specifically about those conversations keeps them up, but only one question\n- Not be mechanical or just repeat back\n\nI want to validate the experience, show I understand the specific pattern (rumination on conversations at bedtime), and perhaps gently invite them to share more about what's happening in those moments - maybe the emotional quality or what about those conversations lingers. I should keep it warm, specific, and not overly clinical.\n\nLet me write a natural, concise counselor response in Korean.\n",
  "started_at": "2026-10-30T05:10:01.872472+00:00",
